  "title": "DHCP: Don't try to finalize a composite TVB with all zero length TVBs",
  "description": "Zero length TVBs aren't added to composite TVBs. Trying to finalize\na composite TVB with no members throws a dissector error. (The code\ncan't really handle it in either case and might crash.)\n\nSo don't create the composite TVB until we get a nonzero option length.\nIf all the options have zero length, there won't be a composite TVB,\nand we can just mark that with an expert info.\n\nFix #20260",
